{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_041: scgpt + ViT-L + transformer + concat, acc=0.507, cost=3.95 GPU-hrs), evidence is very sparse. The most impactful uncertainty is whether the expensive scgpt RNA encoder is actually necessary or whether the cheaper scvi_n200 encoder (a 200-dim VAE) can match its performance. Config_013 isolates this single variable (scgpt→scvi_n200) while holding everything else constant (multimodal, multiprofile, ViT-L, transformer, concat). If scvi_n200 performs comparably, we save ~1-1.5 GPU-hrs per experiment across the remaining 8 runs, freeing budget for more exploratory trials. If it underperforms, we confirm scgpt's value and can focus optimization on other axes (fusion, aggregation, image encoder). This is the highest-information experiment at this stage because the RNA encoder choice affects every future multimodal configuration and carries the largest single cost differential. Expected relative cost: ~65-75% of config_041 (≈2.5-3 GPU-hrs), since scvi_n200 is substantially lighter than scgpt while ViT-L and transformer aggregation remain."
}

